<newsitem itemid="18548" id="root" date="1996-08-28" xml:lang="en">
<title>NETHERLANDS: TELEGRAAF FIRST-HALF NET DOWN 16.5 PCT.</title>
<headline>TELEGRAAF FIRST-HALF NET DOWN 16.5 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    45.4  vs  54.4</p>
<p>    Turnover			     687    vs 613</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    81.4  vs  72.1</p>
<p>Note - Publisher NV Holdingmaatschappij De Telegraaf said in</p>
<p>April it expected 1996 profits to drop sharply as a result of</p>
<p>writing off goodwill on previous takeovers and start-up losses</p>
<p>at its television interests.</p>
<p>    Net financial charges		5.3  vs  10.7 gains</p>
<p>    Tax				     30.8  vs  28.9</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains after tax    0.2  vs   0.4</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		822.0  vs 881.8*</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity	     717.1  vs 723.3*</p>
<p>*NOTE - Comparative figures for balance sheet at end-1995.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
